---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About MelodyMind Knowledge"
  description="How MelodyMind Knowledge researches music history, explains technical terms, creates original audio, and documents AI-assisted editorial work."
  ><article class="reading-shell about">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Knowledge should change what you notice.</h1><p>
      MelodyMind Knowledge is for listeners who encounter a musical term, production
      choice, instrument, or genre and want more than a short dictionary definition.
    </p><h2>What the app covers</h2><p>
      Genre guides connect sound to history, places, scenes, and technical practice.
      Listening guides isolate details that can be difficult to identify in a full
      arrangement. Term pages provide a definition, a visual explanation, an original
      audio example, and specific relationships to other ideas.
    </p><h2>How AI assistance is handled</h2><p>
      AI may assist with research organization, drafting, code, and clearly labeled
      editorial illustrations. MelodyMind reviews the final wording, checks factual claims
      against visible sources, and does not present generated images as historical
      evidence.
    </p><h2>Privacy</h2><p>
      The app has no accounts, analytics, cookies, or saved reader profiles. Interactive
      audio state remains in the current page and disappears when the page is closed.
    </p>
  </article></Layout
>
<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .about h1 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .about p {
    font:
      1.08rem/1.7 Literata,
      Georgia,
      serif;
  }

  .about h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
</style>
